      "text": "🚨On February 27, 2026, at approximately 4:40pm, an AMO Multi-Role Enforcement Aircraft operating off the coast of California detected a vessel of interest 10 miles west of Point Loma. The aircrew coordinated with a Coastal Interceptor Vessel Crew and vectored Marine Interdiction Agents onto the target, resulting in a successful interdiction at 5:00pm. The vessel was stopped without incident, with six individuals onboard, all claiming Mexican nationality. The San Diego Marine Unit seized the vessel, and the subjects were processed for removal.\n\nAttempting to enter the United States by sea is illegal. You will be detected, caught, and arrested. Do not risk your life—do not take to the sea! #BorderSecurity #SanDiego",
      "text_resolved": "🚨On February 27, 2026, at approximately 4:40pm, an AMO Multi-Role Enforcement Aircraft operating off the coast of California detected a vessel of interest 10 miles west of Point Loma. The aircrew coordinated with a Coastal Interceptor Vessel Crew and vectored Marine Interdiction Agents onto the target, resulting in a successful interdiction at 5:00pm. The vessel was stopped without incident, with six individuals onboard, all claiming Mexican nationality. The San Diego Marine Unit seized the vessel, and the subjects were processed for removal.\n\nAttempting to enter the United States by sea is illegal. You will be detected, caught, and arrested. Do not risk your life—do not take to the sea! #BorderSecurity #SanDiego",
